      {
        "id": 138206,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-14T21:30:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You can run pretty much <span class=\"bbcode-i\">any</span> tabletop RPG on a forum, if RPOL (Roleplay Online) is anything to go by…DnD is one of the most popular (that and Pathfinder) in fact. I've also played in a couple of DnD games on an entirely different forum before I joined RPOL (the guy who ran that first DnD game was the one who ended up pointing me at RPOL when someone he knew on there was starting up a game of Mouse Guard and he knew I'd mentioned being interested in it at some point). Really, you just need a bunch of threads (OOC thread, IC thread, maybe a rules thread, stuff like that) and it's helpful if there's also somewhere the GM can store their own resources (though they can just use their own hard drive, I suppose ;)). Having character sheets visible to the GM helps a lot, too. Oh, and in terms of actual gameplay, finding a way to tweak combat so that one round doesn't take about three weeks of real time is kind of useful too ;).</p>",
