      {
        "id": 138211,
        "name": "Craig",
        "username": "Craig",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-17T13:23:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Belle Sorciere\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Belle Sorciere:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So many RPGs. I'd say my favorites have been White Wolf's WoD, Trinity-Aberrant-Adventure!, Scion, Exalted, Scarred Lands. From others: Feng Shui, Fading Suns, Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Icons, BASH!, Shadowrun, Earthdawn, and Eclipse Phase.Fate is currently my favorite thing, although I haven't played much of it yet. The closest I've come is running an Icons game (which is some kind of Fate hybrid), but I am leaning toward straight up Fate, esp. Mecha vs. Kaiju, The Dresden Files, Nova Praxis, several more I am forgetting, and the Fate game being done for the superhero fiction series  Wearing the Cape .</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Capes, Cowls, and Villains Foul is really good, if you like the more storytelling type games. If you've heard of Cartoon Action Hour before, it basically a superhero version of that. For quick pick-up games, that and ICONS are my go-to.</p>",
