        "created_at": "2015-04-21T06:57:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Craig\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/48/2150_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Craig:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Belle Sorciere wrote:</b><br><blockquote>So many RPGs. I'd say my favorites have been White Wolf's WoD, Trinity-Aberrant-Adventure!, Scion, Exalted, Scarred Lands. From others: Feng Shui, Fading Suns, Mutants &amp; Masterminds, Icons, BASH!, Shadowrun, Earthdawn, and Eclipse Phase.Fate is currently my favorite thing, although I haven't played much of it yet. The closest I've come is running an Icons game (which is some kind of Fate hybrid), but I am leaning toward straight up Fate, esp. Mecha vs. Kaiju, The Dresden Files, Nova Praxis, several more I am forgetting, and the Fate game being done for the superhero fiction series Wearing the Cape.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nCapes, Cowls, and Villains Foul is really good, if you like the more storytelling type games. If you've heard of Cartoon Action Hour before, it basically a superhero version of that. For quick pick-up games, that and ICONS are my go-to.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thank you for the recommendation! I've not heard of that. I have heard of Cartoon Action Hour.</p>",
